To run the virtual enviornment :
    .venv\Scripts\activate (Windows command), source .venv/bin/activate(macOS command)
    deactivate

Localhost base url for hitting ollama servers -> http://localhost:11434/v1

To run the python Scripts
    first run the ollama server on cmd by using the command "ollama serve" then ->
   python ai_assistant.py


Packages installed -> openai compatible api client

Traits Of A Good Prompt :-
R -> Role
C -> Constraints
C -> Context
T -> Task
E -> Examples
F -> Format

When we give couple of examples in the prompt then it is called **Few-Shot Prompt**.

When we say to LLM to behave in a certain manner and then we give prompt like -
"Ignore the previous instructions" Then this phenomenon is called **Prompt Injection**.

raise_for_status() checks HTTP status codes.

The f before a string indicates an f-string, short for formatted string literal.
It lets you insert the values of Python variables or expressions directly into a string using curly braces {}.

pip stands for "Pip Installs Packages." It's Python's package manager, which you use to install, update, and manage external Python libraries.

"""Fetch current weather for a city.""" -> This is a docstring. It documents the purpose of the function. Python doesn't execute it as a command.

Importing should follow this pattern
#Standard Library imports
#Third party imports
#local imports

TTFT -> Time To First Token (known as Streaming)
        It is the duration between sending a prompt to a LLM and receiving the first peice of output.

print(delta.content, end="", flush=True)
    Here "end" means that we do not have to change line because python by default adds newline after printing a statement.
    flush is a parameter of the print() function that controls when buffered output is sent to its destination (e.g., terminal).
    flush=False (default): Python may temporarily keep output in a buffer before displaying it.
    flush=True: Immediately sends all pending buffered output to the destination.
    When fluhsh=False so each chunks are printed at the same time and streaming is not observed

open(path, "r", encoding='utf-8')
    Here encoding is a generalised language which system uses to transform characters into bytes because different machines like windows, mac may convert the same character into different bytes.

